My spacing convention is shaped by a set of related observations:
- Blank lines separating logically separate blocks are good
- Blank lines all over the place make blank lines separating blocks 
  worthless
- A line containing a single punctuator at the same indentation level 
  as before it has the same effect as a blank line

Your example code is *full* of what I consider to be blank-line 
